      "flex": "101 1 0%",
      "mods": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "html": "<big><b>SKOL ZERO ZERO</b></big>\nAt some point, alcohol-free beer became part of a world obsessed with self-improvement. A world of cold plunges, morning routines and people who suddenly had a lot to say about their gut health.\nWith the launch of Brazil’s first zero-alcohol, zero-sugar beer, Skol saw an opportunity to have a little fun with all of that.",
        "align": "left"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "flex": "99 1 0%",
      "mods": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "html": "<small><b>Role</b><br>Creative Direction, Art Direction<br><br><b>With</b><br>Bruno Brux, Rainor Marinho, Gabriel Padilha, Vitor Sotero, Samoel Junqueira</small><br><br><small><b>Production</b><br>Lightfarm Studios</small><br><br><small><b>Agency</b><br>GUT<br><br><b>Client</b><br>Skol<br><br><b>Year</b><br>2026</small>",
        "align": ""
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "embed",
    "src": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1230714388",
    "ratio": "56.25%"
   },
   {
    "type": "text",
    "html": "<big>Twenty years after one of Brazil’s most iconic beer campaigns, we brought back Skol’s famous “What if Skol had invented it?” with an entirely new playground: the world of wellness. Turns out healthy habits are a lot more interesting when imagined by a beer brand.</big>",
    "align": "center"
   },
   {
    "type": "grid",
    "items": [
     {
      "w": 960,
      "h": 540,
